# Line endings, pinned.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout converts text files to CRLF — and gofmt then
# flags EVERY .go file, because Go source is LF. CI found exactly that on its
# first run: build, vet and test passed, gofmt failed on all nine files, while
# the same check was clean on the machine that wrote them.
#
# Pinning it here means the answer does not depend on anyone's core.autocrlf.

*.go       text eol=lf
go.mod     text eol=lf
go.sum     text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
LICENSE        text eol=lf

# Never touched: a converted binary is a broken binary.
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
